Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/videotoolbox: declare 32-bit depth for streams with alpha

Not from FFmpeg's master: written for CasparCG's macOS port, and still needed there
(checked 25 October 2026).

The decoder configuration dictionary is also passed as the format description's
extensions, and it carries no kCMFormatDescriptionExtension_Depth. Without it
VideoToolbox decodes a stream with alpha into an RGB output as if opaque: ProRes
4444 with alpha into 32BGRA comes back with alpha 255 everywhere. Measured with
VTDecompressionSession on the same compressed sample: the file's own description
(Depth 32) gives alpha down to 75/255 as encoded, a description without extensions
gives 255 everywhere, and one with Depth 32 alone gives 75 again. AYUV and AYUV64
outputs carry alpha either way, which is why this went unseen.

--- a/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c	2026-10-25 02:07:41
+++ b/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c	2026-10-25 02:07:41
@@ -848,6 +848,19 @@
                             kVTVideoDecoderSpecification_RequireHardwareAcceleratedVideoDecoder,
                          kCFBooleanTrue);
 
+    // This dictionary is also the format description's extensions. Without a depth there,
+    // VideoToolbox decodes a stream with alpha into an RGB output as opaque (32BGRA comes
+    // back with alpha 255 everywhere); its AYUV outputs carry alpha either way.
+    {
+        const AVPixFmtDescriptor *sw_desc = av_pix_fmt_desc_get(avctx->sw_pix_fmt);
+        if (sw_desc && (sw_desc->flags & AV_PIX_FMT_FLAG_ALPHA)) {
+            int depth = 32;
+            CFNumberRef depth_num = CFNumberCreate(kCFAllocatorDefault, kCFNumberIntType, &depth);
+            CFDictionarySetValue(config_info, kCMFormatDescriptionExtension_Depth, depth_num);
+            CFRelease(depth_num);
+        }
+    }
+
     avc_info = CFDictionaryCreateMutable(kCFAllocatorDefault,
                                          1,
                                          &kCFTypeDictionaryKeyCallBacks,
